WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.410
So we're tracking a whole bunch of vaccine
trials and development for Corona virus vaccines.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:10.210
And there's news from a couple of different
vaccine manufacturers or researchers that

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:15.870
I think is relevant, important and potentially
optimistic, which think we could use a little

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:16.870
bit of right now.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.040
So the first one is Oxford University.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.670
Oxford University could have a vaccine ready
to be used in September.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:30.970
The reason that Oxford has a head start is
that they've already been working on a vaccine

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:37.829
for prior corona viruses and they already
have proven of the formula, so to speak, to

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:39.750
be harmless to humans.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.260
From a safety perspective.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:48.290
So Oxford already has a vaccine for this specific
corona virus.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:55.270
Last month in a lab in Montana, they tested
this specific vaccine on rhesus monkeys.

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:57.790
They give the monkeys the vaccine.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:01.250
They expose the monkeys to huge amounts of
the virus.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:05.159
The monkeys without the vaccine all got the
virus.

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:10.569
And more than 28 days later, the six monkeys
that had been vaccinated did not get the virus

00:01:10.569 --> 00:01:11.869
at any point in time.

00:01:11.869 --> 00:01:12.869
That's huge.

00:01:12.869 --> 00:01:19.810
The rhesus monkey is the closest thing to
Homo sapiens for the purposes of testing vaccines.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:21.029
You can read a lot about that.

00:01:21.029 --> 00:01:22.840
If that's interesting to you.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:31.119
Now, is it guaranteed that a vaccine that
is safe in humans and works in rhesus monkeys

00:01:31.119 --> 00:01:33.689
will work just as well to create immunity
in humans?

00:01:33.689 --> 00:01:37.579
No, it's not a guarantee, but it's a very
good sign.

00:01:37.579 --> 00:01:41.829
Next step is human trials of this specific
vaccine.

00:01:41.829 --> 00:01:45.770
They're going to be doing a trial with 6000
people by the end of May.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:49.709
That's very, very big and will be really important
to see how that goes.

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:57.090
Now, the question is, does it work to prevent
Corona virus in humans?

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.849
That's what this six thousand person test
is meant to figure out.

00:02:00.849 --> 00:02:03.159
And a few important things here to think about.

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:04.200
Number one.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.420
OK, how does a vaccine work?

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:11.450
The vaccine contains an element of the germ
that makes people sick.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:18.200
It could be a killed or weakened version of
the germ so that the vaccine doesn't give

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.319
you the disease.

00:02:19.319 --> 00:02:21.110
That would be a disaster.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:24.470
Some vaccines have just part of the germ.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:26.010
It's enough of the germ.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:31.510
The idea is whether it's been weakened or
it's only a part of it or it's dead germ.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:37.260
It's got to be enough that the body reacts
by making antibodies, which then in an ideal

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.599
world makes you immune to the full germ if
you were to be invaded by it.

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:46.319
And you have to go through numerous steps,
including testing the vaccines for safety,

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:51.650
testing the vaccine for efficacy, seeing if
it generates what is the right dose to generate

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:55.040
enough antibodies that you will be immune.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:59.249
You can have a situation where the vaccine
is safe in the sense that it doesn't harm

00:02:59.249 --> 00:03:01.569
humans, but it might not make you immune.

00:03:01.569 --> 00:03:08.560
There can be cases where the vaccine could
make you have a more serious version of the

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:09.560
disease.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:12.329
If you were to be infected, that would be
a disaster, of course.

00:03:12.329 --> 00:03:16.959
So what needs to happen for this vaccine to
be useable in September?

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:19.920
First, you've got to test the six thousand
humans in May.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.950
That has to go well.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:27.050
Number two, there often is a production issue
when it comes to vaccines, because if you

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:32.900
wait until you know it's the vaccine to use
to start production, you're behind and you've

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.939
lost a really important time that could be
used to start vaccinating people.

00:03:36.939 --> 00:03:41.989
So what they're going to do is now or soon
they will start production of this vaccine

00:03:41.989 --> 00:03:45.430
before they even know for sure that it's going
to be the vaccine.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:52.459
This is to be able to have at least some millions
of doses ready as soon as it's determined

00:03:52.459 --> 00:03:54.090
that this is a vaccine that works.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:59.859
And then lastly, important, if it were to
be available in September, it's not going

00:03:59.859 --> 00:04:01.430
to be everybody.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:04.030
And their mother goes and gets this vaccine
in September.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:08.159
If everything goes perfectly in September,
there would be a few million doses.

00:04:08.159 --> 00:04:12.810
It would probably be authorized under emergency
use.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:17.239
And probably at that stage it would just be
for health care, health care workers, which

00:04:17.239 --> 00:04:22.139
makes sense and then subsequently for the
most vulnerable people in populations.

00:04:22.139 --> 00:04:27.919
So this is all good news, but most likely
there will be more than one vaccine that's

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:32.460
used when things get going because of the
number of doses globaly that are going to

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.460
be needed.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.259
So a couple of questions that now come up.

00:04:36.259 --> 00:04:42.990
Will this be like a flu vaccine that's only
effective against like that year's strain

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.190
or mutation answer?

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:46.190
We don't know.

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:50.350
There's a research paper that says that the
vaccine candidates for this.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:58.280
Corona virus would match all circulating strains
of the virus, but not that they would work

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.310
on all corona viruses.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:05.229
That's an important distinction there would
be of the vaccines being worked on now.

00:05:05.229 --> 00:05:10.460
We already have at least my moderately different
strains of this Corona virus that have spread

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:11.810
due to mutation.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:17.610
The vaccine would likely work on all of those,
but it would not work on any corona virus.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:22.020
As you know, there are many corona viruses,
including common colds can sometimes be caused

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.790
by corona viruses.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:29.960
The good news is that Cauvin, 19, seems more
stable than the flu virus.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:33.050
The mutation rate is much lower.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:38.729
That helps hopefully have one that will work
longer than the flu vaccine works.

00:05:38.729 --> 00:05:39.729
It's all speculation.

00:05:39.729 --> 00:05:41.430
We just don't know at this point.

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:43.389
One other bit of hopeful vaccine news.

00:05:43.389 --> 00:05:46.669
So this is the Oxford trial I've been telling
you about.

00:05:46.669 --> 00:05:51.970
The there's a German company working with
Pfizer, which has also started human trials,

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:56.849
and they could potentially have millions of
vaccines ready in the 2020 calendar year.

00:05:56.849 --> 00:05:57.849
Now, that could be November.

00:05:57.849 --> 00:06:02.860
It could be the end of December, but they're
starting tests in the US next week.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:06.830
The idea is emergency use on the table in
the fall.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:10.370
And if they get moving on production soon
before they even know for sure that it'll

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:13.430
work, could have a few million doses available.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:19.590
They say that twelve participants have been
vaccinated since the start of the study on

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:21.199
April 23rd.

00:06:21.199 --> 00:06:22.840
No results yet.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.259
Many things happening.

00:06:24.259 --> 00:06:29.460
One thing I'm going to address at the end
of the show in the voice mail segment is whether

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:44.180
I would want to be at the front of the line
for these vaccines.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:07:33.449
I'll address that in 
a

00:07:33.449 --> 00:07:41.539
little bit.

